MobileNetV4 encoder (chessq-chesscam-mnv4m-320-v1-fp16.tflite,
chessq-chesscam-mnv4m-320-v1-fp32.safetensors):
The encoder starts from the timm library's
mobilenetv4_conv_medium.e250_r384_in12k_ft_in1k weights, Apache License 2.0,
https://huggingface.co/timm/mobilenetv4_conv_medium.e250_r384_in12k_ft_in1k.
MobileNetV4 architecture: Qin et al., "MobileNetV4: Universal Models for the
Mobile Ecosystem", Google, 2024. By PBatch23888: the encoder was trained for
chessboard recognition together with a ChessQueries decoder, using the
ChessQueries code, and exported to LiteRT with FP16 weights.

Training data used under attribution terms:
Fenit: "Annotated Image Dataset for Fenit: Automatic Chessboard Digitization and
FEN Generation", Harjanto, Oei and Susanto, Binus University, CC BY 4.0.
Samryan: chess-dataset by Sam Ryan and Mukund Vaidya, MIT License,
https://github.com/samryan18/chess-dataset.
CVChess labels: released with ChessQueries, CC BY-NC 4.0.
